  "publicationDraft": "Thommy swapped a rib-injured Kamara for Fournette, who gave him seven consecutive starts. Tony waited through Kamara's London absence, got 21.40 points the following week, then packaged him with Gabe Davis for A.J. Brown and James Robinson. Fournette's role diminished as Rachaad White emerged, and Thommy benched him for the rest of the fantasy season. Even a 21.70-point December outing went unused. Thommy bought immediate production; Tony bought a trade chip. The direct scoring gap favors Thommy, but Tony's subsequent deal deserves its own evaluation before anyone calls this a robbery.",
